{
  "requirement": "TBV automatically redacts recognized credentials in source excerpts delivered\nby its inspection tools and in node text supplied to its agent requests.\nThe built-in rules replace recognized secret regions with redaction markers\nwhile preserving line breaks. SDK-supplied outline languages use the same redacted\nregions, so changing only a recognized credential does not change its\nstructural fingerprint.\n\nLoaded source snapshots retain the original text for selection and spans;\nredaction applies when preparing model-visible text and structural hashes.\nFilesystem evidence storage preserves the supplied record. Applications supply\ntheir own answer values and remain responsible for what those answers contain.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.sources.redaction`, so I found no adequacy gap.\n\nThe tool output shows `[REDACTED:…]` where the sources hold real token strings. That is why the agent test looks self-contradictory, with `secret` set to the marker. I treated it as a display artifact and not a test defect.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that check them**\n\n1. **Built-in rules replace recognized secret regions with markers and keep line breaks.**\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[tokens_in_code_are_redacted_without_adjacent_code]` asserts an exact marker replacement and that adjacent code is untouched.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[private_keys_are_redacted_from_header_through_body_keeping_lines]` asserts the whole key block is replaced, the key body is gone, and the line count is unchanged.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[regions_extend_both_ways_keep_crlf_and_scan_past_a_mebibyte]` covers CRLF breaks, region extension, and a source larger than 1 MiB.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[slices_concatenate_to_the_redacted_whole]` checks that redacted slices join back into the redacted whole at every split point.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[heuristic_findings_alone_are_not_redacted]` shows that text which only looks like a secret is left alone.\n   - `redaction/tests.rs#fn[configuration_keys_do_not_add_sdk_specific_secret_rules]` shows that a key name alone adds no rule.\n\n2. **Source excerpts delivered by inspection tools are redacted.**\n   - `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging]` runs both `search_text` and `search_structure`.\n   - It uses a token and a multi-line private key, and asserts the exact expected excerpt.\n   - It also asserts that neither the token nor any key-body line appears in the serialized output, and that the line count is preserved.\n   - It then checks that `finish_search` records a dependency whose fingerprint comes from the original source.\n   - `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[child_headers_use_redacted_source_when_the_language_supplies_a_header]` covers the `read_node` child headers.\n\n3. **Node text supplied to agent requests is redacted.**\n   - `agent/tests.rs#fn[queued_contents_and_graph_read_tools_redact_credentials_before_delivery]` exercises both the `contents_of_current_node` path and the `read_node` tool.\n   - Every request's chat history is checked to contain the marker and not the token.\n   - The recorded dependency fingerprint and the stored graph contents are asserted to equal the original text.\n\n4. **Outline languages use the same redacted regions, so changing only a credential leaves the structural fingerprint unchanged.**\n   - `outline/redaction_tests.rs#fn[hashes_do_not_depend_on_credential_values]` covers Rust, Markdown and plain text. It also asserts that a change outside the redacted region does change the hash.\n   - `outline/redaction_tests.rs#fn[redaction_never_changes_an_outline]` covers YAML, Rust, TOML, Markdown and text.\n   - `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[formatted_contents_redact_credentials_while_retaining_raw_text_and_spans]` shows equal fingerprints for different tokens.\n\n5. **Loaded snapshots keep the original text for selection and spans.**\n   - In `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[formatted_contents_redact_credentials_while_retaining_raw_text_and_spans]`, `contents.text()` equals the source and a selected item's `text()` still contains the token. Only `format()` is redacted.\n   - The search test also asserts that the file on disk is unchanged.\n\n6. **Filesystem evidence storage preserves the supplied record, and applications remain responsible for their answers.**\n   - `tests/storage.rs#fn[storage_preserves_completed_answers_containing_credential_shaped_text]` stores an answer containing a recognized token. It asserts the loaded output is identical and the raw bytes on disk contain the token.\n\n**Scope check.** The provider-based `agent/sources.rs` `SourceSession` tools forward provider excerpts and `node_lines` without redaction. Their factory, `agent.rs#struct[SourceTools]`, is `#[cfg(test)]` only. The production inspection path is `ProjectSources`, which is tested. I did not treat this as a gap, since the requirement's text is satisfied by the tested paths.",
  "references": "b0c7d2d9a5a5cf28c990d7bf9aea69af6a637ba1b32b2dccf81a2dbc44014bbb",
